            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-xl",
            "max_width_desktop": "135ch",
            "richtext": "<p>For elite athletes, sleep isn’t a luxury —it’s a cornerstone of performance. For professional tennis player Jessica Pegula, quality rest is just as important as training, nutrition, and recovery. Between travel, competition, and everyday life, creating the right sleep environment is essential.</p><p>And one of Jessica Pegula’s non-negotiables? Clean, fresh air.</p><h3><strong>Why Sleep Quality Matters for Performance</strong></h3><p>Sleep is when the body repairs muscle tissue, consolidates memory, and restores energy. For athletes like Jessica, even small disruptions such as poor air quality, allergens, or dry air can impact her recovery and readiness the next day.</p><p>“Air quality is one of those things you don’t always think about,” Pegula says. “But it affects everything - from how well you sleep to how you feel when you step on the court.”</p>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "s3"
          }
        },
