            "richtext": "<h3><strong>Creating a Performance-Ready Sleep Environment</strong></h3><p>Jessica’s sleep essentials focus on optimizing her surroundings so her body can do what it does best: recover.</p><p>Key elements include:</p><ul><li><strong>Consistent routines</strong>, even while traveling</li><li><strong>Minimal distractions</strong> and calming bedtime habits</li><li><strong>Clean, filtered air</strong> to reduce allergens and airborne irritants</li></ul><p></p><p>Air quality plays a major role in sleep comfort. Clean, fresh air can help reduce nighttime congestion, coughing, and dryness — all factors that can interrupt deep sleep cycles.</p>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "p2"
          }
        },
